# What Vercel does not upload. A leading / means "this folder at the root". Without it a folder name matches at any
# depth: hero-video/ also dropped media/hero-video/ (the film) and checkout/ dropped api/_lib/checkout/.
# tests/unit/deploy-files.test.mjs checks that everything the site serves or its functions import is uploaded.
/lead-capture/
# The checkout's SQL, setup guide and checks (checkout/README.md); its pages are start/, its functions api/checkout.mjs and
# api/stripe-webhook.mjs.
/checkout/
# The legal pages: their built pages are in legal/; the sources, build and tests stay out of the deployment.
/legal-src/
# The Meta ads page: its built pages are in customers/ (with the Review Race's widget, built in from review-race/public/race),
# and its function is the Review Race's, api/race.mjs. Nothing a function imports lives in meta/, so none of it is
# uploaded; vercel.json redirects /meta/* away as well.
/meta/
# The Review Race (/customers runs it): only its server code is uploaded, because api/race.mjs and api/race-cron.mjs
# import it. Its widget is served from customers/assets/race/; its standalone test page, tests, tools, SQL and docs stay out.
/review-race/public/
/review-race/tests/
/review-race/tools/
/review-race/sql/
/review-race/*.md
/review-race/vercel.json
/review-race/package.json
/review-race/package-lock.json
/review-race/.env.example
/review-race/.gitignore
/review-race/.vercelignore
# The proof system (/admin, case studies): its docs, tests and tools stay out of the deployment.
PROOF.md
/tests/
/tools/
# The story film's sources (script, voiceover, 3D scenes, tools): only what they build, in media/hero-video/, is served.
/hero-video/
# Repository rules and the session hook are for the people and agents working on the repo, not the site.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
